            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The house air tightness is in a fairly good shape and the air leakage is low.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the moment of the audit, we noticed that the wall insulation was R-19. This level is under the actual standard of R-28. We recommend the addition of insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse is requirements. In order to be eligible for the rebate, an addition of a minimum of R-20 is required. The rebate for this addition is 2.50$/square foot. If R-30+ is reached, the rebate is 3.50$/square foot.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the moment of the audit the attic insulation was R-40. We recommend the addition of insulation to meet the standard of R-60. If possible, to reach R-70 is ideal.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>At the moment of the assessment, we noticed that the header joists were not insulated. Therefore, we recommend the insulation of perimeter joist.</foundation>
                <windows>At the moment of the inspection, some windows were double panes. We recommend the replacement of the units by Triple panes windows certified Energy Star. </windows>
                <VentilationSystem>The natural ventilation of the house is very low. We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) certified HVI (Home Ventilation Institute), to insure a proper ventilation in the entire house.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>The home owner expressed some thoughts about changing the supplementary heating system (Toyostove) for a greener heating system. We recommend the installation of an Heat pump for the following reasons:

-Could use 3 times less electricity

-Uses electricity

-No need for fossil fuel

-Some models can also provide cooling options during summer

</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
